Hanumān reasons Sītā cannot feast adorn or heed another --- Hanumān deems sleeper another woman and roams drink hall --- Hanumān sees thousand song-skilled women around bull-like Rāvaṇa --- Hanumān surveys half-eaten meats peacocks and cultured wines --- Hanumān notes gold vessels broken jars and strewn garlands --- Hanumān views embracing sleepers like sleeping lotuses --- Hanumān fears gazing at others wives breaches dharma --- Hanumān keeps pure mind and misses Jānakī among divine maidens
